# The checker's registration passes, in Dawn: the twelve passes that walk a
# module's declarations before a single body is checked, and the helpers only
# they call.
#
# The middle layer of the checker's module DAG (docs/arch-split-design.md
# §2.1): above cx.dawn, below checker.dawn. The cut is the call graph's own --
# the transitive closure of the twelve passes and the closure of body checking
# meet only in the helpers cx.dawn already holds. checker.dawn still calls down
# here (check_module runs the passes in order); nothing here calls back up.

